#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119671 :question/id #uuid "21a6808a-5b1c-5b1d-9bd4-da605fb6d920" :question/math-academy-id "e-6218" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ where\n$$\n\\mathbf{a_1}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{a_2}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{b}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}13 \\\\ - 5 \\\\ k\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}} & =\\mathbf{b} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=13 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{14}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-16{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-11\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = k-11$. Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0 = k-11 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad k=11.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713945 :question-generator/id #uuid "0093edb6-d50b-5cb6-b0ca-3d36b15a57d9" :question-generator/script "generators/7a/7a8549b940191f1b677fdd977781b382224c051052c101283d9dfb11f3de8098/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29ca9bcb-050a-547b-b2da-4f0f41e21511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312293} {:answer/id #uuid "33e4e32f-db84-5c96-add7-afe0ed9eb2ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312393} {:answer/id #uuid "91785332-a99c-5761-adb1-4c713d6b8094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313134} {:answer/id #uuid "921e2a58-090e-5b48-8da8-da76875590bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313147} {:answer/id #uuid "df4042c6-1a0f-5e6e-b14e-7f66d258577b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91785332-a99c-5761-adb1-4c713d6b8094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313134} :answer-field/id #uuid "af7aa591-d12f-5d0b-8d77-aa97493d51fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314484}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "38bc27cb-fe0f-5096-8126-f66c64c344e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-34060" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Span}\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}},{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}} & =\\mathbf{b} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-7 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k-28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k-28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-3.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-3\\,⇒\\,k=3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f85f4b-26f5-50db-b96c-916dbd611e86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339412} {:answer/id #uuid "9d875afa-7e59-51e5-bea6-2f37d23abfc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340550} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e48be0-7bbe-5447-b9bb-2c25b8e944ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340781} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0306d7-4703-5ffa-a07a-b6e35b29e543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340816} {:answer/id #uuid "fcbbf23a-a8fc-5115-9c28-cac86f2b465b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd0306d7-4703-5ffa-a07a-b6e35b29e543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340816} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac17a9f0-71f7-58cc-b12b-dc681a6d7fcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341680}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f53bb678-a419-585c-a65e-c61f25afddb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74560" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Span}\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}},{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}} & =\\mathbf{b} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2} &=-12 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2} &=-10 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-3 & 9 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 7 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 18 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+24\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+24.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+24\\,⇒\\,k=-24.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28acedc8-6185-5174-a20f-1523f6e81664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238413} {:answer/id #uuid "911bf0a4-bca6-575a-8b8e-b3222ff2700c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239312} {:answer/id #uuid "aa49ecea-790f-512b-a264-3f8fef658cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239546} {:answer/id #uuid "deff7940-817f-5ec1-8070-a43c35299f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240003} {:answer/id #uuid "e11c88b3