left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-45\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+45\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+45.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+45\\,⟹\\,k=-45.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b030142-b351-5e7f-9981-3a7a900479a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339506} {:answer/id #uuid "a7085a93-27ed-53b5-a303-a8fca730844d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340645} {:answer/id #uuid "b4affd08-9db3-5c2c-982f-d4b5ce542718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340767} {:answer/id #uuid "cbcdc6a7-206d-5669-bb3f-7c2d9331e8e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340934} {:answer/id #uuid "df5e0a81-5e66-52e1-bec5-63012c9a7c11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7085a93-27ed-53b5-a303-a8fca730844d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340645} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb292a0b-9d7e-5720-a326-a1c46c9f7bf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341737}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d5c520f5-835e-5cc8-a0fb-53c3d5239f5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74597" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b}\\in \\text{Span}\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}},{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}} & =\\mathbf{b} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k+6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds t