R_2\\leftarrow \\left(\\frac{1}{7}\\right)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k + 7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row represents $0x_1+0x_2=k + 7$. Consistency therefore requires\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 &=k + 7 \\\\ k &=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot equations give $x_2=3$ and $x_1=2$. These values also establish sufficiency:\n\n$$\n(2)\\mathbf{a}_1+(3)\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=-7$ is the only value for which the vector lies in the span."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ff86def-1312-55f6-b9f9-9f26573d47b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713915} {:answer/id #uuid "6303f35e-cd3b-5731-bcc9-b47df12f1b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713922} {:answer/id #uuid "7e43fea9-8a97-5285-ac05-6fc3caf99f40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713925} {:answer/id #uuid "813750cb-49a0-5f58-a080-ba16e2bc4e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713926} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ae45cb-4f67-5134-a583-25e87f006421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "813750cb-49a0-5f58-a080-ba16e2bc4e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713926} :answer-field/id #uuid "32f73196-a68b-5046-a31f-9f29ca235cb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713918}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77197499-69ac-5e2d-a2ca-305941aed072" :question/problem "Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$, where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ exactly when $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ has a solution. Equating coordinates gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2 x_{1} - 2 x_{2} &=10 \\\\ - 2 x_{1} - 3 x_{2} &=10 \\\\ - 4 x_{1} - 6 x_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nForm the augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 10 \\\\ -4 & -6 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_1\\leftarrow \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 10 \\\\ -4 & -6 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(-2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 20 \\\\ -4 & -6 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(-4)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 20 \\\\ 0 & -10 & k + 20\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow \\left(- \\frac{1}{5}\\right)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -10 & k + 20\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(-10)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k - 20\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row represents $0x_1+0x_2=k - 20$. Consistency therefore requires\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 &=k - 20 \\\\ k &=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot equations give $x_2=-4$ and $x_1=1$. These values also establish sufficiency:\n\n$$\n(1)\\mathbf{a}_1+(-4)\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=20$ is the only value for which the vector lies in the span."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ad62b4a-99ba-540f-9