{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nPlace the two known-coordinate equations first (a row permutation).\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 14 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_1\\leftarrow \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & 7 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -4 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & 7 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -20 \\\\ 4 & -4 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(4)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & 7 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -20 \\\\ 0 & -10 & k - 28\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow \\left(- \\frac{1}{5}\\right)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -10 & k - 28\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(-10)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k + 12\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row represents $0x_1+0x_2=k + 12$. Consistency therefore requires\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 &=k + 12 \\\\ k &=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot equations give $x_2=4$ and $x_1=1$. These values also establish sufficiency:\n\n$$\n(1)\\mathbf{a}_1+(4)\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=-12$ is the only value for which the vector lies in the span."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713951 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fc457f3-38b7-51fd-843f-acc46b625e5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713947} {:answer/id #uuid "3312b576-841b-5973-a098-6dffa81d4259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713950} {:answer/id #uuid "63bd2b78-9fb0-544c-8088-14db533f917c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713953} {:answer/id #uuid "996d3431-d5ff-5929-8c7b-1f491d133