\\\\ 0 & 0 & k + 10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row represents $0x_1+0x_2=k + 10$. Consistency therefore requires\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 &=k + 10 \\\\ k &=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot equations give $x_2=-4$ and $x_1=-1$. These values also establish sufficiency:\n\n$$\n(-1)\\mathbf{a}_1+(-4)\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=-10$ is the only value for which the vector lies in the span."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713957 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29588c26-3d32-53a3-811d-a9b384d88e49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713948} {:answer/id #uuid "731be95a-e18d-587d-9dd3-33e7be3691ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713956} {:answer/id #uuid "9aa2390e-5cba-5aee-a2ac-de3cb860e307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713962} {:answer/id #uuid "a01d252a-eba6-51eb-96ba-a661b9090e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713965} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a5b744-2253-5e47-baea-84704a410b2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "731be95a-e18d-587d-9dd3-33e7be3691ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713956} :answer-field/id #uuid "2faf3b52-72d2-537c-b7e2-61ca4195695e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713949}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73a64046-9fa9-5d82-aceb-991b0070c493" :question/problem "Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$, where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}k \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the augmented matrix for $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ to determine when the system is consistent:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -4 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ exactly when $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ has a solution. Equating coordinates gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}- 2 x_{1} - 4 x_{2} &=k \\\\ x_{1} + x_{2} &=2 \\\\ - x_{1} - 2 x_{2} &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nForm the augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -4 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nPlace the two known-coordinate equations first (a row permutation).\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -4 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -4 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(-2)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & k + 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow (-1)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & k + 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(-2)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k + 10\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row represents $0x_1+0x_2=k + 10$. Consistency therefore requires\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 &=k + 10 \\\\ k &=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot equations give $x_2=3$ and $x_1=-1$. These values also establish sufficiency:\n\n$$\n(-1)\\mathbf{a}_1+(3)\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=-10$ is the only value for which the vector lies in the span."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cca7a7f-be72-5fe2-89fb-f27cf987024d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713955} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee3e626-42b6-5d81-864f-227fe56de9c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713963} {:answer/id #uuid "a14b32c3-107a-5ea0-925c-b35b2d0a6052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713966} {:answer/id #uuid "a93ec8bc-2528-5884-8701-fb18e58628f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713969} {:answer/id #uuid "c213984e-21e9-51f9-85f6-130f380887b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c213984e-21e9-51f9-85f6-130f380887b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713970} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c07838c-a244-579a-97cb-1676a12ea83f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713954}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "996f5bdf-6de3-5168-a1d0-b97c26e1ea47" :question/problem "Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$, where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the augmented matrix for $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ to determine when the system is consistent:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\operatorname{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ exactly when $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ has a solution. Equating coordinates gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}- x_{1} - x_{2} &=3 \\\\ x_{1} + 2 x_{2} &=-3 \\\\ x_{1} + 2 x_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nForm the augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_1\\leftarrow (-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & k\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k + 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3-(1)R_2$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k + 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe last row represents $0x_1+0x_2=k + 3$. Consistency therefore requires\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 &=k + 3 \\\\ k &=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot equations give $x_2=0$ and $x_1=-3$. These values also establish sufficiency:\n\n$$\n(-3)\\mathbf{a}_1+(0)\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=-3$ is the only value for which the vector lies in the span."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "140ce550-6f64-57a7-96b1-bbcedd684765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713946} {:answer/id #uuid "42d31477-2c22-55c4-b7d6-1e7217b62522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713952} {:answer/id #uuid "74b8af6b-4af7-5064-bb89-04e67b5c3ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713958} {:answer/id #uuid "7e321976-0226-5cb5-83ec-c5751c4e21c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713959} {:answer/id #uuid "c6173ec0-b